^CONVERSION ERROR$
could not fully type-check
^Symbol\.+: std::num_get<wchar_t,std::tag-istreambuf_iterator<char,
^Symbol\.+: std::num_get<char,std::tag-istreambuf_iterator<wchar_t,
--
Conversion-level gate for std::regex construction: the body of the
_Compiler recursive-descent parser must be present (a `$tmp` of
_M_disjunction exists only when its body was converted); the converting
move constructor `shared_ptr<const _NFA>(shared_ptr<_NFA>&&)` odr-used
by _Compiler::_M_get_nfa must have a body (it was bodiless in one
candidate order: the already-instantiated const& specialization and
the && deduction placeholder tied, then the ODR-used member was never
queued); and no HYBRID facet instantiation such as
num_get<wchar_t, istreambuf_iterator<char>> may exist (a default
template argument bound to an enclosing instantiation's same-named
parameter, [temp.param]/14).  In the vacuous layouts described in
test.desc the _Compiler constructor was bodiless and none of the _M_*
compiler members were even instantiated.
